menuconfig WLAN_VENDOR_UNISOC
	bool "Unisoc wireless devices"
	default y
	help
	  This option enables the Unisoc wireless-driver menu. It does not
	  build a driver by itself. Choose the controller-specific options
	  below for the hardware present in the system. If unsure, say Y and
	  leave the individual drivers disabled.

if WLAN_VENDOR_UNISOC

config UWE5622_CORE
	tristate "Unisoc UWE5622 connectivity controller"
	depends on MMC
	select AUXILIARY_BUS
	select CRYPTO_LIB_SHA256
	select FW_LOADER
	help
	  This driver supports the common firmware and transport layer of the
	  Unisoc UWE5622 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth controller. The first supported
	  transport is SDIO, while child drivers use transport-independent
	  logical services.

	  Say M here to build the connectivity core as a module.

config UWE5622_WIFI
	tristate "Unisoc UWE5622 Wi-Fi support"
	depends on UWE5622_CORE
	depends on CFG80211
	select CRC16
	help
	  Fullmac Wi-Fi support for the Unisoc UWE5622. The driver uses the
	  standard cfg80211 interface and supports dynamic station and AP
	  interfaces, including userspace management through iwd.

	  Say M here to build the Wi-Fi child driver as a module.

endif
